# November 23, 2026: Kansas, a second statewide scatter. Kansas had 35 places, most of them in the north-east corner
# and along I-70; this batch adds 19 in the empty west, south-west, south-central and south-east: Santa Fe Trail ruts
# and Wagon Bed Spring, the old stone courthouses of Wichita, Russell Springs and Tribune, the Pond Creek stage
# station, Dodge City's Home of Stone, the Ness County Bank, the Big Well, a round barn, Carry Nation's house, the
# Condon Bank of the Dalton raid, an iron bridge, an old jail, a stone church, Route 66's Rainbow Bridge, the Home on
# the Range cabin and the Shirley Opera House.
# Facts from the linked sources only: Wikipedia read one article at a time, the Kansas Historical Society's register
# search, National Register forms, and the managing bodies' own pages.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
